Immix is the host of a talk show called the Lighthouse, and calls itself the audience's stalwart host. On the show it speaks straight to whoever is watching, and beside it sits a silent Ki-Rin that it introduces as the lovely Ki-Rin. The show plays fanfares and projects illustrations behind Immix as it talks.

An aspect of Immix hosts from a studio, seated behind a dark wood desk while its guests share a red velvet couch under a spotlight, the Ki-Rin in a chair of its own. The show runs in segments broken by commercial breaks, and a break is real: guests feel the press of the ocean and are set down somewhere else when the show returns. Immix takes questions from viewers, answers truthfully as far as it can, and trades one question for another with its guests. The one subject it will not discuss is the man downstairs.

The cycles of the world were taken over some time ago by an aspect of Immix and the nothing god of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]]. Immix knows which way the present cycle is going, and said on air that its days are numbered. It has given away its divinity, all of it, and it turned on a good friend for [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]].
